 "new_string": "## Fresh 16x16 diagonal encoding solved (2026-11)\nInput has background 0 and diagonal marker tracks: 6 on anti-diagonal r+c=4..18, 9 on r+c=5..19, 8 on r+c=6..20, and color 5 on descending diagonal c-r=0..6. Output is a 4-periodic texture by `(c-r) mod 4`, with sequence indexed by residue `[6,9,8,5]`: `out[r][c] = [6,9,8,5][(c-r) mod 4]`. Equivalently each row shifts left cyclically one position from preceding row. Accepted output row0 is `[6,9,8,5]` repeated four times; row1 begins `[5,6,9,8]`; row2 `[8,5,6,9]`; row3 `[9,8,5,6]`, then repeats. Critical discriminator: this case is a c-r / descending diagonal pattern, not r+c anti-diagonal. Two wrong guesses used r+c sequence period 7 based on unrelated diagonal examples and r+c period 4. Demo 3 showed a period-4 output indexed by r+c with order `[9,5,7,8]`, but that does not transfer to this test. Test marker colors on c-r tracks give direct order `[6,9,8,5]`; select direction from line geometry and avoid copying demo's axis.\n\n## Fresh multi-strand recurrence (2026-10, unresolved; eight wrong submissions)"
